														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839082">
									

<p>Let's see what we have here.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My primary concern is that you don't have a story. Like, what happens with the object? How do they use it? Who made it? Where do you want to go with it? SCP articles nowadays have some kind of story to go along with it, and this seems to be just the object. This makes it to feel like a Series I article, and that is not good. Those types of articles are very old, and are usually frowned upon nowadays.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, you really need to add some kind of story to this.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

